OL,3,GNEWSAVolunteers complete restoration of
OL,4,AD-Day aircraft
OL,5,
OL,6,FThree members of a Herefordshire
OL,7,Faviation group have spent five years
OL,8,Fpainstakingly restoring a military
OL,9,Faircraft they believe flew over Gold
OL,10,FBeach during the D-Day landings.
OL,12,FThe Auster aircraft, which was used as
OL,13,Fan artillery spotter during World War
OL,14,FTwo, had fallen into disrepair before
OL,15,Fit was brought to Shobdon in 2021.
OL,17,FVolunteers from the Shobdon Historical
OL,18,FAircraft Group have now completed the
OL,19,Frestoration and hope to see the plane
OL,20,Freturn to the skies in spring 2027.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,356,350,200,160,0,100
